From: Mihawk <163614687+mihawk-99@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 06:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: PS5: GetCurrentProcessorNumber says the CPU the thread runs on, within the count Wine reports

The console's libc has no sched_getcpu, so NtGetCurrentProcessorNumber took Wine's last fallback: the first processor
in the thread's affinity mask, 0 for every thread (tests/cpu-count-probe.c on the base PS5, 2026-11-03: 32 busy
threads, number_seen=1). A program that keeps per-processor data (allocators, job systems) put every thread on the
same slot.

It now reads RDTSCP's processor id, the CPU the thread runs on, as Windows' own GetCurrentProcessorNumber does, and
numbers it within the CPUs Wine reports (WINE_CPU_TOPOLOGY's list): a thread can run on a CPU outside the list (a
helper's threads are widened to the console's 16 while the title lists 13), and a number not below the count reads
past a per-processor table sized by it. The same CPU always gives the same number.
---
  dlls/ntdll/unix/thread.c | 20 ++++++++++++++++++++
  1 file changed, 20 insertions(+)

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/thread.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/thread.c
index 2282575..4a19afc 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/thread.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/thread.c
@@ -2848,6 +2848,26 @@ ULONG WINAPI NtGetCurrentProcessorNumber(void)
         return cpu_id;
     }
 #endif
+#if defined(__PROSPERO__) && defined(__x86_64__)
+    /* PS5: no sched_getcpu, and the fallback below gave every thread processor 0. RDTSCP's processor id is the CPU the
+     * thread runs on (Windows' own GetCurrentProcessorNumber reads it too). It is numbered within the CPUs Wine reports:
+     * a thread may run on one outside them (a helper's threads are widened to the console's 16), and a number not below
+     * the count reads past a game's per-processor table. The same CPU always gives the same number. */
+    {
+        struct cpu_topology_override *override = get_cpu_topology_override();
+        unsigned int aux, cpu, i;
+
+        __asm__ __volatile__( "rdtscp" : "=c"(aux) : : "eax", "edx" );
+        cpu = aux & 0xfff;
+        if (override && override->cpu_count)
+        {
+            for (i = 0; i < override->cpu_count; ++i)
+                if (override->host_cpu_id[i] == cpu) return i;
+            return cpu % override->cpu_count;
+        }
+        if (peb->NumberOfProcessors) return cpu % peb->NumberOfProcessors;
+    }
+#endif
 #if defined(__APPLE__) && (defined(__x86_64__) || defined(__i386__))
     {
         struct {
